  "notes": "Lafayette Avenue: name printed west of the strip (about x 2000-2300) and at Lafayette Circle to the east; inside the strip only AVENUE is printed on the diagonal. Its unlabelled arm east of Clifton Avenue (centre y about 3385) is taken as the same street, so that crossing is recorded as a cross. Egbert Avenue ends at Amazon Avenue (T); Amazon runs on east to Clifton Avenue beyond the overlap. Belsaw Place is a rectangular loop (Lot A, 40 ft) with a narrow entrance lane (about 15 ft, y 4918-4940) to Clifton Avenue; a second narrow strip marked 6 in. W. PIPE from the loop's north-east corner to Clifton at about (5380, 4378) is read as a pipe strip, not a street. Greendale and Woolper: suffix not seen inside the overlap, Avenue assumed. Dell Eva Lane name read east of the overlap (about x 6300). Middleton, Clifton and McAlpin carry a solid water-pipe line inside the roadway; centres are between the lot lines. McAlpin's south edge is at the plate cut, centre y uncertain by about 10 px."
